From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:56:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: sample microSD data
 as the vendor does

With latch clock 1 alone the tuning still settles on a data delay of
about 45 cells, and reads fail CRC at the same rate or worse. Written at
runtime, a data delay of 8 with latch clock 1 failed as before with one
CKGEN stage (24 of 1063 reads) and not at all with none (0 of 1054).

Set no CKGEN stage and limit the tuning to 32 steps so that it chooses
a short delay.

Needs the mtk-sd ckgen-delay change. Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts    | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index ebb7c3b..28b745e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -751,12 +751,14 @@
 	vmmc-supply = <&mt6351_vmch_reg>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&mt6351_vmc_reg>;
 	/*
-	 * Latch read data one internal clock later, as the vendor kernel
-	 * does. With latch 0 the tuning settles on about 47 delay cells,
-	 * and reads that start after the bus has been idle fail CRC a few
-	 * percent of the time although the tuning block passes.
+	 * Sample read data as the vendor kernel does: latch one internal
+	 * clock later, no CKGEN stage and a short pad delay. The tuning
+	 * block also passes at delays of 33-61, but real reads there fail
+	 * CRC a few percent of the time, so keep the scan to 0-31.
 	 */
 	mediatek,latch-ck = <1>;
+	mediatek,ckgen-delay = <0>;
+	mediatek,tuning-step = <32>;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
 	status = "okay";
